---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="Privacy" description="How this site uses cookies and analytics.">
  <article class="post">
    <h1>Privacy</h1>
    <!-- DRAFT: review before relying on this. -->
    <div class="prose">
      <p>This is a personal site. I don't sell, share or use your data for advertising.</p>

      <h2>Analytics</h2>
      <p>
        If you accept cookies, I use Google Analytics to understand how people find and use the site,
        such as which pages are read and roughly where visitors come from. Google Analytics sets cookies
        to tell visits apart. If you choose "Necessary only", no analytics cookies are set. Google may
        still receive basic, cookieless signals that don't identify you, under Google's Consent Mode.
      </p>
      <p>
        You can change your choice at any time using the "Cookie preferences" link at the bottom of
        every page. Google's own privacy policy is at
        <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" rel="noopener">policies.google.com/privacy</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Things saved in your browser</h2>
      <p>
        The site remembers your cookie choice and, if you use the toggle, whether you prefer light or
        dark mode. Both are stored in your own browser and never sent to me.
      </p>

      <h2>Embedded videos</h2>
      <p>
        The Media page embeds YouTube videos using YouTube's privacy-enhanced mode. YouTube may store
        information in your browser once you play a video.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>Questions about any of this: <a href="mailto:rob@toolproof.com.au">rob@toolproof.com.au</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>
